{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Ensure adoptees are given equal status in any forced adoption redress.",
        "additional_details": "The July 2026 apology about historical forced adoption in England, accepted harm extended beyond the direct victims (Prime Minister's Statement to the House of Commons on 2nd July 2026). The \u00a34 million support scheme does not mention redress or commitment to adoptees sharing equally in one. A scheme in the Australian state of Victoria excluded adoptees. The Government must not repeat that omission. We seek a firm timetable on NHS England issuing guidance to GP's on adoption trauma.",
        "background": "We urge the Government to recognise adoptees, their children and grandchildren as equal victims of historical forced adoption, and to give them equal financial terms in any future redress scheme, which should be a statutory redress scheme to avoid litigation needs.",
